-- title:
--   Magnitude bounds for all intermediate lists of the HvdH reference step
-- statement:
--   Let $K \ge 20$, $N \ge 2^{2^{8K}+1}$, $q = \mathrm{mkParams}(K,N)$ and $x, y\in\mathbb N$. There is an explicit bound $B_q = 2\max(2^p, B_W)\,c_S^K$ with $B_q < 2^P$ and $\mathrm{size}(B_q) \le p + \lfloor p/8\rfloor$ such that every intermediate list of `refStep q x y` has all (real and imaginary) entries bounded by $B_q$ in absolute value: (a) the CRT digit vectors `rU q x`, `rU q y` and their scaled complex versions `ecU`; (b) every stage of the Gaussian-resampling ($\tilde S$) passes of the three forward transforms (inputs $U$, $V$ and the pointwise product $W$) and every stage of the $\tilde B$ passes; (c) the inputs of the Fermat convolution and the chirp table `chirpL q`; (d) every `convL` and `FtL` output (and every `fermatW` output is bounded by $2^P$); (e) the products $W$, $Y$; (f) the output of `exactConvL` and the `crtOut` digits.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** `LB L B` (resp. `LBz`) says every pair (resp. integer) in the list has absolute values $\le B$; `tensorGo (axs.take k) dims` is the list after the first $k$ axis passes. All list functions (`refStep`, `fwdL`, `FtL`, `convL`, `fermatW`, `exactConvL`, `crtIn/crtOut`, `tensorGo`) are those of the published `Def_IntMul_HvdH_MachineRef`. These bounds size the registers of the machine implementation.
-- source:
--   D. Harvey, J. van der Hoeven, Integer multiplication in time O(n log n), Ann. of Math. 193 (2021), 563–617 (Theorem 1.1: multitape Turing machine multiplication in O(n log n)). Lemma `NLogN.BD.refStep_LB_mkParams` of the Lean development NLogN/HBd3.lean (lines 361–460), written for the prove2.me integer-multiplication campaign.

